From: Claude <noreply@anthropic.com>
Date: Sat, 24 Oct 2026 08:09:49 +0000
Subject: [PATCH 3/5] e2e run: the production site process (E2ESiteProcess)
 builds the routed runtime too

The plumbing run with a fake lexical judge (0 calls reached the server)
showed that E2ESiteProcess, the class the e2e run actually starts, overrides
SiteProcess.__init__ and kept runtime=None, so --routing never took effect;
its inherited close() then failed on the missing attribute, which broke every
run from fa609166. Runtime construction is now SiteProcess._make_runtime, used
by both classes, and close() tolerates its absence.

Co-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>
Claude-Session: https://claude.ai/code/session_01Cc9kurj5azoGuhPNUVde8U
---
 research/e2e_ingest/site_graph.py      |  5 +--
 research/routing_spike/site_process.py | 43 ++++++++++++++------------
 2 files changed, 27 insertions(+), 21 deletions(-)

